0..78 Comment "// The globular theory at dimension one, its associator a stated law, modelled"
79..104 Comment "// by the circle\'s paths."
105..107 Comment "//"
108..182 Comment "// A stated law is the theory\'s generator cell: no rule orients it, and no"
183..255 Comment "// default fills its component. The Path reading is a model of the cells"
256..316 Comment "// reading, so `std.math.path`\'s associator writes the cell."
317..319 Comment "//"
320..398 Comment "// The model writes the right unit law by conversion and the associator by the"
399..483 Comment "// theorem. A model leaving the associator out has it discharged by `Path.here`: the"
484..528 Comment "// two nestings of a chain of paths convert."
529..531 Comment "//"
532..614 Comment "// - see: `pathological/higher-cells/path-cells.gandr` — a model of the naturals"
615..675 Comment "//   leaving the cell out, and a scope breaking a stated law"
676..750 Comment "// - see: `cat-shape.gandr` — the same theory with its associator a rule"
752..799 Comment "// `assoc`, the associator of path composition."
